        <p style="text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:10pt"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif"><strong>2025 Impairment Test of Discontinued Operations</strong></span></span></p>
        <p style="text-align:justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:10pt"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif">For the year ended December 31, 2025, all the Company's goodwill was associated with the Cannabis Business. As such, the Company assessed the goodwill and long-lived assets of each of the Cannabis Business for indicators of impairment. While no indicators of impairment were noted, the Company determined the fair value of the disposal group was less than the carrying value of the net assets.&#160;The carrying value of the TruHC reporting unit was $<ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260227111019042" name="us-gaap:Assets" contextRef="C_20250926_usgaapEquityInterestIssuedOrIssuableByTypeAxis_zstkTwoThousandTwentyFiveImpairmentTestOfDiscontinuedOperationsMember_usgaapReportingUnitAxis_zstkTruhcReportingUnitMember" unitRef="USD" scale="6" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">4.9</ix:nonFraction> million, comprised mainly of goodwill of $<ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260227111058282" name="us-gaap:Goodwill" contextRef="C_20250926_usgaapEquityInterestIssuedOrIssuableByTypeAxis_zstkTwoThousandTwentyFiveImpairmentTestOfDiscontinuedOperationsMember_usgaapReportingUnitAxis_zstkTruhcReportingUnitMember" unitRef="USD" scale="6" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">2.2</ix:nonFraction> million and licenses of $<ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260227111111729" name="us-gaap:OtherIntangibleAssetsNet" contextRef="C_20250926_usgaapEquityInterestIssuedOrIssuableByTypeAxis_zstkTwoThousandTwentyFiveImpairmentTestOfDiscontinuedOperationsMember_usgaapReportingUnitAxis_zstkTruhcReportingUnitMember" unitRef="USD" scale="6" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">2.5</ix:nonFraction> million. Because the fair value of the disposal group was less than the carrying amount of the net assets, the Company recorded an impairment of $<ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260227111137754" name="us-gaap:GoodwillImpairmentLoss" contextRef="C_20250901to20250926_usgaapEquityInterestIssuedOrIssuableByTypeAxis_zstkTwoThousandTwentyFiveImpairmentTestOfDiscontinuedOperationsMember_usgaapReportingUnitAxis_zstkTruhcReportingUnitMember" unitRef="USD" scale="6" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">1.4</ix:nonFraction> million within the commercial and wholesale segment. This item was recorded in the loss from discontinued operations, net of taxes caption on the unaudited condensed interim consolidated statements of loss and comprehensive loss.&#160;</span></span></p>
        <p style="text-align:justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:10pt"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif"><strong>Other Long-Lived Asset Impairment Tests for the year ended December 31, 2025</strong></span></span></p>
        <p style="text-align:justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:10pt"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif">As discussed in Note 15, the Company had been subleasing retail space in Miami, Florida to a third party since the third quarter of 2023. The Company is leasing this retail space pursuant to a lease agreement that expires in November 2026, which is the same term as the sublease agreement. In March 2025, the sublessor informed the Company that it planned to terminate the sublease agreement, effective in May 2025. The Company considered this to be an indicator of impairment, and, thus, performed a quantitative analysis as of March 31, 2025 to determine if impairment existed by comparing the carrying amount of the operating lease right of use asset to the future undiscounted cash flows the asset is expected to generate over its remaining life. This analysis indicated the asset values may not be recoverable. The Company then calculated the fair value of this asset using an income approach. As a result, the Company recorded an impairment of operating lease right of use assets within its corporate asset group and segment totaling less than $<ix:nonFraction id="Fxbrl_20260220222924754" name="zstk:ImpairmentOfOperatingLeaseRightOfUseAssets" contextRef="C_20250101to20251231_usgaapEquityInterestIssuedOrIssuableByTypeAxis_zstkTwoThousandTwentyFiveOtherLongLivedAssetImpairmentTestMember" unitRef="USD" scale="6" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">0.1</ix:nonFraction> million. These charges were recorded in the asset impairment caption on the consolidated statements of loss and comprehensive loss. The Company has found a new sublessor for this space under an agreement with similar payment terms as the original sublease. Therefore, there were no further indicators of impairment as of December 31, 2025.</span></span></p>
        <p style="text-align:justify;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:10pt"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif"><strong>2024 Impairment Test of Discontinued Operations</strong></span></span></p>
        <p style="text-align:justify;margin-top:10pt;margin-bottom:10pt"><span style="font-size:10pt"><span style="font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif">The Company qualitatively assessed whether it is more likely than not that the fair value of TruHC is less than its carrying amount, including goodwill. Based on that assessment, the Company determined that this condition, for TruHC, does not exist. As such, performing the first step of the two-step test impairment test for TruHC was unnecessary.</span></span></p>
